# === dsh-deepartments patch: dsh-llm-deepseek tool-call consecutiveness strip (STAGE 2) ===
#
# WHAT THIS FIXES
#   STAGE 2 of the defense-in-depth series, applied ON TOP of the stage-1
#   orphan role:'tool' sweep (patches/dsh-llm-deepseek-orphan-sweep.patch).
#   The strict DeepSeek direct API requires tool responses to CONSECUTIVELY
#   follow the assistant message that issued the tool_calls (one immediate
#   set - no interleaved user/system messages). A dept_sleep close under
#   Fix A can leave [assistant(tool_calls) -> user(journal) -> tool(result)]
#   on the wire (the deferred sleep-replace map is in-memory and empty after
#   a process restart), and the strict validator rejects that interleave with
#   a 400 "insufficient tool messages following tool_calls". This stage adds a
#   post-pass to BOTH serializers of the installed @deepseek-ai/dsh-llm-deepseek
#   lib:
#     - serializeMessages           (plain path)
#     - serializeMessagesWithImages (image/vision path)
#   For every assistant wire message with tool_calls, the post-pass collects
#   the tool responses that follow CONSECUTIVELY (until the first non-tool
#   message); if any tool_call_id lacks its consecutive response, it STRIPS
#   the whole tool_calls array from that assistant (text/reasoning kept) and
#   drops the tool responses of the stripped calls (they would otherwise be
#   orphaned {role:'tool'} messages - the stage-1 400 class). Clean consecutive
#   pairs pass through byte-identical (never mutated; verified by probe in
#   .dsh/reports/builder/2026-08-21-patch-toolcall-strip.md).
#
# TARGET FILE (after dsh upgrade, in the global install tree)
#   <npm-root>/@deepseek-ai/dsh/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm-deepseek/lib/index.js
#   Diff base: the STAGE-1-patched file (md5 da90e47fccdeae16f93472159aee0e1c).
#   The patch is self-contained (relative paths a/lib/index.js b/lib/index.js);
#   scripts/reapply-dsh-patches.sh rewrites them to the resolved absolute path
#   before applying.
#
# FINGERPRINTS (md5)
#   f82d2ea38a6a27ae0c7f691d384b3949  pristine @deepseek-ai/dsh 0.1.1-rc.2 lib/index.js (78 334 B)
#   da90e47fccdeae16f93472159aee0e1c  stage 1 applied (orphan sweep, 78 712 B) - the BASE this patch applies onto
#   3390675e5d48a82fe906ba365d91713f  stage 2 applied (this patch, tool-call strip)
#   Restoration backups: /opt/dsh/backups/llm-deepseek-index.js-* (see patches/README.md)
#
# WHY NOT UPSTREAM
#   Owner decision: fold as a repo patch, no upstream PR (same as stage 1).
#   The fix lives inside the installed dsh tree and is lost on every dsh
#   upgrade -> re-apply after each upgrade with scripts/reapply-dsh-patches.sh
#   (fingerprint-gated; stages 1+2 chained, each verified).
#
--- a/lib/index.js
